<section class="sc-recognition" data-dark="true" data-screen-label="Does this sound like you">
<div class="sc-recognition__inner">
<div class="sc-recognition__head">
<div>
<span style="display:inline-block;margin:0 0 18px;padding-top:14px;border-top:2px solid var(--sand-500);font-size:11px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:var(--ls-eyebrow);text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--sand-500)">Does this sound familiar?</span>
<h2>What Leads Patients to Explore Regenerative Treatment</h2>
</div>
<p>People rarely arrive here because they simply want a new procedure. Usually, they are trying to solve a very practical problem while avoiding an expensive or poorly understood decision.</p>
</div>
<div class="sc-recognition__grid">
<article class="sc-recognition__item"><span class="sc-recognition__num">01</span><p>Knee pain is still limiting you despite physiotherapy, medication or previous injections.</p></article>
<article class="sc-recognition__item"><span class="sc-recognition__num">02</span><p>You have been told your osteoarthritis is progressing and want to understand what options remain.</p></article>
<article class="sc-recognition__item"><span class="sc-recognition__num">03</span><p>Knee replacement has entered the conversation, but you want to know whether reasonable non-surgical options are still worth discussing.</p></article>
<article class="sc-recognition__item"><span class="sc-recognition__num">04</span><p>You received a stem-cell, BMAC or PRP proposal and are not sure how to compare it with another clinic's protocol.</p></article>
<article class="sc-recognition__item"><span class="sc-recognition__num">05</span><p>You would consider travelling for treatment if there were a meaningful medical, quality or cost reason to do so.</p></article>
<article class="sc-recognition__item"><span class="sc-recognition__num">06</span><p>You are willing to invest in your health, but you want evidence and transparency before committing.</p></article>
</div>
<div class="sc-recognition__close">
<p><strong>If one or more of these sounds familiar, the next step is not choosing a clinic.</strong> It is understanding which options are actually worth discussing for your knee. These situations do not establish medical candidacy.</p>
<button class="sc-inline-cta on-dark" data-stemcierge-quiz="true" type="button">Review My Knee Treatment Options</button>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section data-screen-label="Candidacy" id="candidate" style="background:var(--paper);padding:clamp(56px,7vw,104px) 0;scroll-margin-top:120px">
<div style="width:min(100% - clamp(64px,14vw,128px),1200px);margin-inline:auto">
<span style="display:inline-block;margin:0 0 18px;padding-top:14px;border-top:2px solid var(--sand-500);font-size:11px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:var(--ls-eyebrow);text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--sand-700)">Could it make sense for your knee?</span>
<h2 style="margin:0;max-width:26ch;font-family:var(--font-body);font-weight:700;font-size:clamp(31px,3.9vw,52px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:var(--ink-950)">Who Might Be Considered for Cell-Based Treatment?</h2>
<p style="margin:22px 0 0;max-width:70ch;font-family:var(--font-body);font-size:18px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">There is no universally established “ideal stem-cell candidate.” Clinical-trial inclusion criteria should not be turned into a universal treatment algorithm.</p><p style="margin:14px 0 0;max-width:72ch;font-family:var(--font-body);font-size:17px;line-height:1.72;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">For someone with confirmed knee OA, persistent symptoms despite conservative care and realistic expectations, <strong>it may still be reasonable to discuss regenerative options with a qualified physician.</strong> The purpose of evaluation is to determine whether there is a credible option worth considering for your specific knee, not to assume treatment is appropriate.</p>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(300px,1fr));gap:24px;margin-top:clamp(32px,4vw,48px)">
<article style="background:var(--white);border:1px solid var(--line-on-light);border-radius:8px;padding:clamp(26px,3vw,34px);box-shadow:var(--shadow-card-light)">
<div style="width:36px;height:36px;border-radius:var(--radius-circle);display:grid;place-items:center;border:1px solid var(--sand-500);color:var(--sand-700);margin-bottom:20px"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" strokelinecap="round" strokelinejoin="round" strokewidth="2" style="width:17px;height:17px" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="m5 12 4 4 10-10"></path></svg></div>
<h3 style="margin:0 0 16px;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:20px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.3;color:var(--ink-950)">A useful evaluation may consider</h3>
<ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">
<li style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:flex-start;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line-on-light)"><i style="width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--sand-500);display:block;flex:0 0 auto;margin-top:8px"></i>confirmed diagnosis and imaging</li>
<li style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:flex-start;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line-on-light)"><i style="width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--sand-500);display:block;flex:0 0 auto;margin-top:8px"></i>pain severity and functional limitation</li>
<li style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:flex-start;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line-on-light)"><i style="width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--sand-500);display:block;flex:0 0 auto;margin-top:8px"></i>joint alignment and stability</li>
<li style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:flex-start;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line-on-light)"><i style="width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--sand-500);display:block;flex:0 0 auto;margin-top:8px"></i>meniscus and associated pathology</li>
<li style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:flex-start;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line-on-light)"><i style="width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--sand-500);display:block;flex:0 0 auto;margin-top:8px"></i>previous conservative treatment</li>
<li style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:flex-start;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line-on-light)"><i style="width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--sand-500);display:block;flex:0 0 auto;margin-top:8px"></i>health conditions and medications</li>
<li style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:flex-start;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line-on-light)"><i style="width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--sand-500);display:block;flex:0 0 auto;margin-top:8px"></i>activity level and treatment goals</li>
</ul>
</article>
<article style="background:var(--white);border:1px solid var(--line-on-light);border-radius:8px;padding:clamp(26px,3vw,34px);box-shadow:var(--shadow-card-light)">
<div style="width:36px;height:36px;border-radius:var(--radius-circle);display:grid;place-items:center;border:1px solid var(--line-on-light-strong);color:var(--text-on-light-muted);margin-bottom:20px"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" strokelinecap="round" strokewidth="2" style="width:16px;height:16px" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18"></path></svg></div>
<h3 style="margin:0 0 16px;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:20px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.3;color:var(--ink-950)">Biologic treatment may not solve</h3>
<ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">
<li style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line-on-light)"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" strokelinecap="round" strokewidth="2" style="width:16px;height:16px;flex:0 0 auto;margin-top:4px;color:var(--text-on-light-muted)" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18"></path></svg>severe mechanical deformity</li>
<li style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line-on-light)"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" strokelinecap="round" strokewidth="2" style="width:16px;height:16px;flex:0 0 auto;margin-top:4px;color:var(--text-on-light-muted)" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18"></path></svg>major joint instability</li>
<li style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line-on-light)"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" strokelinecap="round" strokewidth="2" style="width:16px;height:16px;flex:0 0 auto;margin-top:4px;color:var(--text-on-light-muted)" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18"></path></svg>problems requiring physical reconstruction</li>
<li style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line-on-light)"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" strokelinecap="round" strokewidth="2" style="width:16px;height:16px;flex:0 0 auto;margin-top:4px;color:var(--text-on-light-muted)" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18"></path></svg>infection or major contraindications</li>
<li style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line-on-light)"><svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" strokelinecap="round" strokewidth="2" style="width:16px;height:16px;flex:0 0 auto;margin-top:4px;color:var(--text-on-light-muted)" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18"></path></svg>advanced structural disease where established surgery is appropriate</li>
</ul>
</article>
</div>
<div style="margin-top:24px;border:1px solid var(--line-on-light-strong);border-radius:8px;padding:clamp(24px,3vw,32px);display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:24px;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between">
<div style="max-width:66ch">
<strong style="display:block;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:20px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.35;color:var(--ink-950)">An X-ray grade alone should not decide the treatment.</strong>
<p style="margin:8px 0 0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">NICE recommends considering joint-replacement referral based on symptoms, function, quality of life and response to non-surgical treatment rather than relying on an arbitrary numerical severity score.<a href="#ref-13" style="font-size:.72em;vertical-align:super;margin-left:2px">13</a></p>
</div>
<button class="sc-inline-cta on-light" data-stemcierge-quiz="true" type="button">Review My Knee Treatment Options</button>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section data-screen-label="Stem cells vs replacement" id="replacement" style="background:var(--white);border-top:1px solid var(--line-on-light);padding:clamp(56px,7vw,104px) 0;scroll-margin-top:120px">
<div style="width:min(100% - clamp(64px,14vw,128px),1200px);margin-inline:auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(320px,1fr));gap:clamp(32px,4vw,64px);align-items:stretch">
<div>
<span style="display:inline-block;margin:0 0 18px;padding-top:14px;border-top:2px solid var(--sand-500);font-size:11px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:var(--ls-eyebrow);text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--sand-700)">A common decision point</span>
<h2 style="margin:0;font-family:var(--font-body);font-weight:700;font-size:clamp(31px,3.9vw,52px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:var(--ink-950)">Stem Cells vs Knee Replacement</h2>
<p style="margin:22px 0 18px;max-width:64ch;font-size:17px;line-height:1.72;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)"><strong>They solve fundamentally different problems.</strong> Cell-based treatment attempts to influence symptoms or joint biology while preserving the existing joint. Knee replacement physically reconstructs the damaged joint surfaces.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 18px;max-width:64ch;font-size:17px;line-height:1.72;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">Current evidence does not establish that stem-cell therapy predictably prevents someone from eventually needing knee replacement. The more useful question is whether a reasonable non-surgical option still exists for your diagnosis, symptoms and goals.</p>
<p style="margin:0;max-width:64ch;font-size:17px;line-height:1.72;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">Established care for knee OA still includes therapeutic exercise, weight management when appropriate, medication strategies and surgery when symptoms substantially impair quality of life and non-surgical care is ineffective or unsuitable.<a href="#ref-13" style="font-size:.72em;vertical-align:super;margin-left:2px">13</a></p>
</div>
<div style="min-height:320px;height:100%;border:1px solid var(--line-on-light);border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--paper)">
<div class="sc-original-visual-slot is-rect" id="knee-replacement-decision" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover"><span class="slot-label">Visual placeholder</span><strong>Warm editorial photo: an active adult walking or on stairs, everyday mobility</strong><small>Replace with a final editorial image or purpose-built infographic before publishing.</small></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section data-dark="true" data-screen-label="Safety and regulation" id="safety" style="background:var(--ink-950);color:var(--white);padding:clamp(56px,7vw,104px) 0;scroll-margin-top:120px">
<div style="width:min(100% - clamp(64px,14vw,128px),1200px);margin-inline:auto">
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(320px,1fr));gap:clamp(32px,4vw,64px);align-items:start;margin-bottom:clamp(36px,4vw,56px)">
<div>
<span style="display:inline-block;margin:0 0 18px;padding-top:14px;border-top:2px solid var(--sand-500);font-size:11px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:var(--ls-eyebrow);text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--sand-500)">Safety &amp; regulation</span>
<h2 style="margin:0;font-family:var(--font-body);font-weight:700;font-size:clamp(31px,3.9vw,52px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:var(--white)">Risks, Safety and FDA Status</h2>
</div>
<div>
<p style="margin:0;max-width:64ch;font-size:17px;line-height:1.72;color:var(--text-on-dark-secondary)">Safety needs to be separated into two questions: <strong>what happened in controlled trials</strong> and <strong>what risks arise in the commercial marketplace.</strong></p>
</div>
</div>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(300px,1fr));gap:24px">
<article data-light="true" style="background:var(--white);border-radius:8px;padding:clamp(26px,3vw,34px);box-shadow:var(--shadow-card-dark)">
<h3 style="margin:0 0 14px;font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:400;font-size:26px;line-height:1.15;color:var(--ink-950)">What clinical studies tell us</h3>
<p style="margin:0 0 14px;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">Serious treatment-related events have generally been uncommon in modern randomized trials, including MILES. However, Cochrane considers the overall safety evidence uncertain because serious events are rare, follow-up is limited and products vary.<a href="#ref-1" style="font-size:.72em;vertical-align:super;margin-left:2px">1</a><a href="#ref-3" style="font-size:.72em;vertical-align:super;margin-left:2px">3</a></p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">Injection-related pain, swelling, inflammatory reactions and infection remain relevant procedural risks.</p>
</article>
<article data-light="true" style="background:var(--white);border-radius:8px;padding:clamp(26px,3vw,34px);box-shadow:var(--shadow-card-dark)">
<h3 style="margin:0 0 14px;font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:400;font-size:26px;line-height:1.15;color:var(--ink-950)">What commercial treatment adds</h3>
<p style="margin:0 0 14px;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">Safety can also depend on sourcing, sterility, processing, manufacturing standards, storage, administration and patient selection. The FDA has reported serious adverse events associated with unapproved regenerative products.<a href="#ref-11" style="font-size:.72em;vertical-align:super;margin-left:2px">11</a></p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">A safety record from one clinical-trial product should not automatically be transferred to every commercial treatment with a similar label.</p>
</article>
</div>
<div style="margin-top:20px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(240px,1fr));gap:clamp(24px,3vw,40px);border:1px solid var(--line-on-dark);border-radius:8px;padding:clamp(26px,3vw,34px)">
<div style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(28px,3vw,38px);line-height:1.1;color:var(--white)">FDA status</div>
<div style="grid-column:span 2;min-width:0">
<p style="margin:0;font-size:16px;line-height:1.72;color:var(--text-on-dark-secondary)"><strong>No regenerative medicine therapy is currently FDA-approved in the United States for orthopedic conditions including osteoarthritis or knee pain.</strong><a href="#ref-11" style="font-size:.72em;vertical-align:super;margin-left:2px">11</a> That is a US regulatory statement, not a universal global rule. International status depends on the country, product, processing, indication and route of administration. ISSCR recommends rigorous clinical investigation and appropriate regulatory oversight for novel cell-based interventions.<a href="#ref-12" style="font-size:.72em;vertical-align:super;margin-left:2px">12</a></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
